<title>HONG KONG: Min Xin Holdings 1996 net up 49.44 pct.</title>
<headline>Min Xin Holdings 1996 net up 49.44 pct.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-25</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year ended December 31</p>
<p>(in million HK$ unless stated)</p>
<p>    Shr (H.K. cents)	   17.63	vs  11.89</p>
<p>    Dividend (H.K. cents)    5.0	  vs  5.0</p>
<p>    Exceptional items	  25.36 gain vs  15.33 loss</p>
<p>    Net			    52.59	vs  35.19</p>
<p>    Turnover		     198.85     vs  154.23</p>
<p>    Company name		 Min Xin Holdings Ltd</p>
<p>    Books close		  June 20-26</p>
<p>    Dividend payable	   July 18</p>
<p>NOTE - Min Xin Holdings engages in investment holding, property investment, finance, banking and insurance.</p>
<p>The company proposed one bonus warrant for every five shares held. Each bonus warrant will entitle the holder thereof to subscribe initially HK$5.38 in cash, subject to adjustment, for one new share at any time between the first dealing day and December 31, 1999, both dates inclusive.</p>
<p>Net is after an exceptional gain of HK$82.49 million on disposal of investment properties, loss of HK$37.67 million on provision for rental receivable from subletting and loss of HK$19.45 million on writeoff of renovation costs.</p>
<p>Total dividend for year is five H.K. cents vs same.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6368</p>
</text>
